# Grey heron

The grey heron is the common large heron of Europe and temperate Asia, standing
motionless at the edge of a river or a fish pond. It hunts by waiting: it stands
in shallow water and catches fish with a downward stab of the bill, taking
whatever passes within reach of a bird that never leaves the surface. Frogs,
voles and ducklings are caught as readily when fish are scarce, and a heron will
hunt a dry field far from water. It nests colonially in tall trees. See
[[ardeidae]].
